# Collapsible studio control sections

Status: DONE
Milestone: Compact control-panel navigation
Dependencies: 05_STUDIO_AND_LAUNCH.todo

## Purpose
Reduce scrolling by allowing every numbered control-panel section to expand or collapse
independently without recreating controls or changing the running tracking session.

## Tasks
- [x] Use a shared collapsible container for all seven numbered sections.
- [x] Start with Input open and the remaining sections folded.
- [x] Add always-visible Expand all and Collapse all actions.
- [x] Support header mouse/keyboard activation and safe focus when controls are folded.
- [x] Preserve control values and widget identity; folding is not a disconnect or debug toggle.
- [x] Complete native layout/keyboard/scroll checks, documentation and artifact handoff.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every numbered section can be toggled independently, with its state visibly indicated.
- [x] Collapsed section bodies stop taking up layout space, including at the minimum window size.
- [x] Collapse all returns the scroll view to the top; toolbar actions remain visible.
- [x] Folding controls preserves their settings and the active runtime.
- [x] New previews, scoped evidence and guide reflect the compact layout.

## Completion evidence
- Focused tests:39cases in collapsible sections, video controls and CLI/runtime modules.
-19native studio groups and9model groups passed, including retained replay and debug windows.
- Initial native layout:2088pxfully expanded,780pxdefault,273pxall collapsed.
- Keyboard Space/Enter, focused-child handover, independent toggles and minimum1020x720layout passed.
- No tracking, rendering, camera/credential handling, model, or recording changes.
- Current native previews and handbook updated; aggregate receipt:
  docs\evidence\collapsible-sections-validation.json.

